tory\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years from 1951 to 2025, and September to October and October to November each came in under 90% of normal in 35 of those years. In 2025, November to December finished at 32% of normal on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids. So far in 2026, March to April sits at 41% of normal on the middle of the grids, and April to May at 111%.</p>"}
